PART 5: MULTI-FORM INPUT DATA PATTERNS
================================================================================

PATTERN 1: FLAT STRUCTURE
================================================================================

const [formData, setFormData] =
  useState({

    field1: '',

    field2: '',

    field3: '',

    field4: ''

  })


Good when:

• Form fields are logically simple

• Deep nesting provides little benefit

• Generic handling is straightforward


================================================================================
PATTERN 2: GROUPED / NESTED STRUCTURE
================================================================================

const [formData, setFormData] =
  useState({

    personal: {

      firstName: '',

      lastName: ''

    },


    contact: {

      email: '',

      phone: ''

    }

  })


Input name:

name="personal.firstName"


Generic nested handler:

const handleChange = (
  event
) => {

  const {
    name,
    value
  } = event.target


  const [
    section,
    field
  ] = name.split('.')


  setFormData(previousData => ({

    ...previousData,

    {

      ...previousData[section],

      value

    }

  }))
}


================================================================================
NESTED UPDATE FLOW
================================================================================

name:

personal.firstName


        ↓


split('.')


        ↓


section:

personal


field:

firstName


        ↓


Previous State


        ↓


Copy Top-Level Object


        ↓


Copy personal Object


        ↓


Update personal.firstName


