================================================================================
CONDITIONAL DATA DECISION
================================================================================

Suppose:

accountType = company

companyName = Contoso


Then user changes:

accountType = individual


The Company Name control disappears.


Question:

Should:

companyName = 'Contoso'


remain in formData?


Possible policies:

OPTION A:
Keep it

OPTION B:
Clear it


Choose based on business requirements.

Do not let hidden stale data accidentally reach submission if the application
does not expect it.


================================================================================
PATTERNS TABLE
================================================================================

+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+
| PATTERN                 | USE CASE                                   |
+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+
| Flat Object             | Straightforward forms                     |
| Nested Object           | Domain-oriented sections                  |
| Mixed Types             | Checkbox + text + select etc.             |
| Validation              | Field-level business rules                |
| Dynamic Fields          | Variable repeated controls                |
| Conditional Fields      | Show/hide based on state                  |
| Array of Objects        | Addresses/contacts/items                  |
| Dependencies            | One field influences another              |
| Async Validation        | Server-dependent checks                   |
+-------------------------+--------------------------------------------+


================================================================================
FLAT VS NESTED STATE
================================================================================

FLAT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
  firstName: '',
  lastName: '',
  street: '',
  city: ''
}


Advantages:

• Simple generic handler

• Fewer nested copies

• Easy for modest forms


NESTED:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
  personal: {
    firstName: '',
    lastName: ''
  },

  address: {
    street: '',
    city: ''
  }
}


Advantages:

• Can mirror domain structure

• Related properties grouped together


Trade-off:

Nested immutable updates require more care.


