================================================================================
KEY TAKEAWAY
================================================================================

A scalable multi-input React form commonly follows:

FORM CONTROLS
      ↓
name + value / checked
      ↓
GENERIC CHANGE HANDLER
      ↓
STRUCTURED formData
      ↓
VALIDATION
      ↓
SUBMISSION


For a flat form:

setFormData(previous => ({

  ...previous,

  nextValue

}))


For nested data:

setFormData(previous => ({

  ...previous,

  {

    ...previous[section],

    nextValue

  }

}))


The goal is not simply to put every field into one large object.

The goal is to choose a state structure that keeps:

DATA
+
UPDATES
+
VALIDATION
+
SUBMISSION

clear and maintainable.


